{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"USN-9213-1","published":"2026-11-26T16:54:17Z","modified":"2026-11-27T04:43:25.841570247Z","related":["UBUNTU-CVE-2026-109089","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-109090","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-93542","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-93543"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-109089","CVE-2026-109090","CVE-2026-93542","CVE-2026-93543","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-109089","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-109090","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-93542","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-93543"],"summary":"libxi vulnerabilities","details":"Adam Bedard discovered that libXi did not properly validate\nDEVICE_RESOLUTION replies from the X server, which could result in a heap\nbuffer overflow. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause\napplications using libXi to crash, resulting in a denial of service.\n(CVE-2026-109089)\n\nAdam Bedard discovered that libXi did not properly allocate memory when\nhandling DEVICE_ENABLE replies from the X server. A remote attacker could\npossibly use this issue to cause applications using libXi to crash,\nresulting in a denial of service. (CVE-2026-109090)\n\nIt was discovered that libXi did not properly validate class data in XI2\nreplies and events. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to\ncause applications using libXi to crash, resulting in a denial of service.\n(CVE-2026-93542)\n\nIt was discovered that libXi did not properly validate class metadata in\nXI2 replies and events. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to\ncause applications using libXi to crash, resulting in a denial of service.\n(CVE-2026-93543)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"libxi","ecosystem":"Ubuntu:22.04:LTS","purl":"pkg:deb/ubuntu/libxi?arch=source&distro=jammy"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2:1.8-1ubuntu0.1"}]}],"versions":["2:1.7.10-1build2","2:1.7.10-1build3","2:1.8-1","2:1.8-1build1"],"ecosystem_specific":{"availability":"No subscription required","binaries":[{"binary_name":"libxi6","binary_version":"2:1.8-1ubuntu0.1"}]},"database_specific":{"cves_map":{"cves":[{"id":"